#NEXUS

[ zhang2024a_fig7: Sauropodomorph tree with small pies on every node, read with the image as it stands (root at left). Most of it is a long ladder whose verticals run a few pixels apart and pass behind the neighbouring pies; each node was read by the rule the drawing follows (every pie sits halfway between its two children), which places every ladder tip without ambiguity: e.g. Mussaurus branches from the node above Seitaad's, its vertical hidden behind that node's pie. Substitute for gorscak2016a_fig6_4, whose doubled verticals the image alone does not settle. Picked case (pie charts on nodes; not a sample, not for accuracy estimates). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only; the pies and squares are not encoded. 56 tips, 0 polytomies. ]

